title: Genesis 11 – The Tower of Babel
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 11: the tower of Babel, the nations scattered, the generations of Shem to Abram, and how God judges nations and heals their land.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-11-tower-of-babel.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 11 study
# (posts 6700, 6701, 6725, 6726, 6730, 6731, 6732). The separate study of January 31, 2023 is its own deck,
# genesis-11-spirit-of-babylon. Fixed: "gibboram" -> "gibbor"; "uncle to Lot" -> "grandfather of Lot" (Genesis 11:27);
# Abraham "170" -> "175" (Genesis 25:7); "morning" -> "mourning".

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 11 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 11: The Tower of Babel
sub: One Language • The Tower • Scattered • Shem to Abram
refs: Genesis 11:1-32
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The tower
--- One Language, and One Speech
kicker: vv. 1–4
sub: Let Us Make Us a Name
scripture: Genesis 11:1-4 | mark: let us build us a city and a tower, whose top may reach unto heaven; and let us make us a name
p: About 100 years after the flood, in the year of Peleg’s birth (*for in his days was the earth divided*), the people imagined a vain thing. A tower to Heaven. That they could work their way to Heaven and be like God. [[Genesis 10:25]]

--- The {Lord} Came Down
kicker: vv. 5–7
sub: Go To, Let Us Go Down
scripture: Genesis 11:5-7 | mark: now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do; Go to, let us go down
p: The {Lord} God, the Father, says, “*let us go down*…” [[Genesis 1:26]]

--- The {Lord} Scattered Them
kicker: vv. 8–9
sub: Therefore Is the Name of It Called Babel
scripture: Genesis 11:8-9 | mark: So the LORD scattered them abroad from thence upon the face of all the earth
p: And they scattered the people and confused their language. We are meant to be in nations. Nations by clan. By blood. Not one world government, full of vanity. Not even by a civic nationalism of paper and statutes that erases who we are, *making a name for ourselves, lest we be scattered abroad upon the face of the whole earth*.

--- That They All May Be One
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 11:6
fig: John 17:20-21 | John 17:20-21 | Not the people made one in vanity to make a name for themselves, but those which believe on Him through His word, one in the Father and the Son.
fig: John 17:22-23 | John 17:22-23

--- Nimrod
kicker: Genesis 10:8–10 • The Founder of Babel
sub: A Mighty Hunter Before the {Lord}
scripture: Genesis 10:8-10 | mark: the beginning of his kingdom was Babel
p: Nimrod gets a bad rap. Having founded Babel and being a mighty man, a hunter before the {Lord}, it is assumed he’s the impetus for the construction of the tower. Most of the assumption is based on his proximity, greatness, being a *gibbor* or mighty man, and his lineage forming the great cities listed in Genesis 10: Babel, Erech, Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar. Some translate his name as “deserter,” others “he rebelled,” and take this to build an entire story around him, the tower, and great wickedness against God. Yet scripture doesn’t give a negative accounting of him.

=== The generations of Shem
--- The Generations of Shem
kicker: vv. 10–11
sub: Shem Begat Arphaxad Two Years After the Flood
scripture: Genesis 11:10-11
p: And then we are given the generations of Shem. The genealogy of man after the flood is again given to establish where and when we are for the next phase of the story being told: the origins and chronology of the people whom God dealt with. Adam to Noah. Noah to Abram. [[Genesis 5:1]]
callout: Many overlook this as simply a history or chronological device, and try to extract much deeper meaning from it than is there, often at the expense of believing it literally, especially the timing of years.

--- Arphaxad, Salah, and Eber
kicker: vv. 12–17
sub: The Line of Shem Continues
scripture: Genesis 11:12-17

--- Peleg, Reu, and Serug
kicker: vv. 18–23
sub: In His Days Was the Earth Divided
scripture: Genesis 11:18-23
note: Peleg: “for in his days was the earth divided.” [[Genesis 10:25]]

--- Nahor and Terah
kicker: vv. 24–26
sub: The Life Spans of Man Shrinking
scripture: Genesis 11:24-26
p: Note that the life spans of man are shrinking as we go from Shem to Abram, approaching the 120 year average God decided back in Genesis 6. Abraham would be 175 when he died. A shadow of the 900 years most of the earlier patriarchs lived to. [[Genesis 6:3]] [[Genesis 25:7]]

--- The Generations of Terah
kicker: vv. 27–32
sub: Terah, Father of Abram
scripture: Genesis 11:27-32 | mark: Terah begat Abram, Nahor, and Haran; and Haran begat Lot
p: The generations of Shem lead to Terah, father of Abraham and grandfather of Lot.

--- From Adam to Jesus
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 11:10
fig: Luke 3:38 | Luke 3:38 | In like manner, the Gospels have similar genealogies, bringing us to Jesus Christ, that we have a lineage and time frame from Adam to Jesus’ earthly incarnation.
fig: Matthew 1:17 | Matthew 1:17
refs: Luke 3:23-38

=== God judges nations
--- God Is No Respecter of Persons
kicker: Application • Nations
sub: The Same Offer of Salvation to All
scripture: Acts 10:34-35
p: God is not a respecter of persons, the Bible says repeatedly. He does not care if you are great or small, rich or poor, man or woman, Greek or Jew, where you’re from or who your parents are. He gives us all the same offer of salvation and adoption in Christ. As individuals, we have free will.

--- God Does Judge Nations
kicker: Application • Nations
sub: Judging Ungodly Nations, Including Our Own
p: God does judge nations. He does favor some over others at times, and destroys many who go too far astray. He curses the land stained by blood of violence, sodomy, fornication. Of people, collectively, to the fourth generation. [[Numbers 35:33]] [[Exodus 34:7]]
callout: We are to know the judgment of God and emulate it. Not being a respecter of persons, giving the Gospel to whomever we meet, but judging ungodly nations for what they are. Including our own. Every nation carries that burden, where the godly among them must turn towards God so that He may heal their land.

--- Scattered Among the Heathen
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 11:8
fig: Leviticus 26:33 | Leviticus 26:33
fig: Deuteronomy 4:26-27 | Deuteronomy 4:26-27

