--- A Remnant According to the Election of Grace
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 11:8
fig: Romans 11:5 | Romans 11:5
fig: Romans 11:7 | Romans 11:7
refs: Romans 11:5-8

--- A Remnant According to the Election of Grace, continued
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 11:8
fig: Jeremiah 6:30 | Jeremiah 6:30 | Speaking of the Jews who would reject the coming Messiah: Romans 1 applies to them as it applies to all that go the way of the Pharaoh. By their individual free will. Collectively judged. [[John 12:40]] [[Romans 1:28]] [[1 Thessalonians 2:14-16]]
note: The whole doctrine is in [[lesson:topic-reprobate|The Reprobate Mind]].

=== If my people
--- If My People
kicker: Application • 2 Chronicles 7:14
sub: How We Save Our Nation
scripture: 2 Chronicles 7:14
p: Unsaved men often criticize born again believers as “doing nothing,” or that we are “weak,” “afraid” or “cowardly,” because we aren’t running around in panic, getting sucked into reactionary spirals by the provocations of the rulers of the darkness of this world. They rail and demand we join seditions and take vengeance for ourselves. But God is clear on how we save our nation and get His blessings for our people.

--- This Is Not “Doing Nothing”
kicker: Application • 2 Chronicles 7:14
sub: Discipline, Motivation and Perseverance
p: Have faith. Obey the commandments. As much as possible, live peaceably among men. Be a godly husband, raise godly children and share the gospel, winning souls. Give comfort to those mourning, be a good judge for the fatherless and true widows. [[Romans 12:18]]
callout: This is not “doing nothing.” It is hard work, or else it wouldn’t be so difficult to get people to do it. Like most effective things, it requires discipline, motivation and perseverance. It’s easier to express impotent outrage online.

--- We Wrestle Not Against Flesh and Blood
kicker: Application • Ephesians 6:12
sub: Fearful for Nothing Except God
scripture: Ephesians 6:12
p: The frustrations and provocations assailing us are how Satan tempts us, so he can accuse the saints before God: to make us sin over it, so that we can be persecuted for those sins by the powers that be. As a people, if Christians turn towards God and obeying Him, fearful for nothing except God, He will hear us and heal our land, and bring blessings to all our nation, believers or not. [[Revelation 12:10]]

--- Stop Doing Nothing and Believe
center: Just being loving and kind, while maintaining the separation and sanctification God asks of us, is a dissident, revolutionary act. When we live blamelessly, it heaps coals upon their heads. But that all requires our faith. So stop doing nothing and believe. [[Romans 12:20]]
